      ],
      "kind": "book",
      "label": "A History of the Valley",
      "model": "book_shelf",
      "codex": "barovia_valley_history",
      "text": "A dry, careful history of the valley. Centuries ago a warlord named Strahd von Zarovich drove out the armies of a rival and claimed these mountains for his family; the people who live here now are the descendants of those he ruled. The author adds, in a nervous footnote, that the valley's lord has never been seen to age, and that it is wise not to write about him at night."
    },
    {
      "id": "library_odd_shelf",
      "cell": [
        4,
        8
      ],
      "kind": "examine",
      "label": "a bookcase",
      "model": "bookcase"
    },
    {
      "id": "strahd_letter",
      "cell": [
        4,
        11
      ],
      "kind": "book",
      "label": "a letter signed S",
      "model": "letter",
      "codex": "death_house_strahd_letter",
      "dialogue": "death_house/house:strahd_letter",
      "text": "Gustav. Your devotion has been noted, and declined. You mistake me for a god who answers prayers; I am a lord who collects what he is owed. Your circle of candles and borrowed Latin will not buy you a single extra year, let alone eternity. Should it ever amuse me, I may come to dinner. Do not set a place. S."
    },
    {
      "id": "durst_deeds",
      "cell": [
        3,
        11
      ],
      "kind": "examine",
      "label": "a bundle of deeds",
      "model": "papers",
